Vertical 2:3 scrapbook travel-journal collage poster themed around [Shanghai]. The centerpiece is enormous, glossy 3D sculptural Chinese characters spelling "[上海]", rendered in cream color with metallic beveled edges, rounded corners, and deep inset windows showing vivid miniature cityscape scenes: the Shanghai skyline, Oriental Pearl Tower, skyscrapers, waterfront night views, historic Bund architecture, Nanjing Road neon signs, riverboats, and warm sunset-to-night lighting.

Characters: Exactly five Japanese-style cute chibi travel bloggers with round faces, beige travel outfits, bucket hats or caps, backpacks, and camera accessories:
- One seated on an upper-left ledge near the Oriental Pearl Tower holding a camera;
- One walking on the upper-right holding a folded map;
- One standing in the center-lower area exploring the 3D text;
- One larger traveler in the bottom-left foreground holding a camera while walking;
- One in the lower-right sitting or leaning beside an orange suitcase.

Collage elements:
- Top-left: vintage postcard stamp reading "SHANGHAI" with a circular overlapping airplane passport stamp;
- Top-center: handwritten title with Chinese "旅行日志" and English "Travel Diary";
- Top-right: taped note with handwritten Chinese romantic travel text and doodled heart, a black vintage camera sticker, and a circular passport stamp reading "SHANGHAI / 上海 / 20.24.05.20";
- Right: "I ♥ SH" sticker;
- Left side: handwritten itinerary checklist with six destination bullets: "东方明珠", "外滩", "南京路步行街", "田子坊", "武康大楼", "迪士尼乐园", dotted route arrows, and text "Have a nice trip!";
- Bottom-left: boarding pass with "PVG", gate, seat, and Shanghai details;
- Bottom-center: small red luggage label reading "上海 / SHANGHAI", and handwritten Chinese note: "下一站，上海 遇见更好的自己" with tiny smiley doodles;
- Bottom-right: postcard reading "SHANGHAI / The City / That Holds / All My Dreams" featuring a mini skyline photo.

Visual style: Bright dreamy sky-blue background with fluffy clouds, Japanese soft-cute Q-version illustration blended with polished 3D typography, pastel tones, warm highlights, washi tape, and paper textures.

A cinematic vertical historical figure archive poster of [班超], featuring a heroic ancient Chinese frontier general breaking out of a documentary-style infographic layout, 3:4 aspect ratio.

Main Subject: In the center foreground, a full-body armored commander in a low-angle heroic pose. He wears detailed layered dark lamellar armor, engraved belt plates, leather boots, and a red-brown cloak billowing to the left, with a dignified expression. His left arm thrusts forward toward the viewer holding a tall wooden command tablet carved with Chinese calligraphy; his right hand grips a vertical ceremonial standard with a tassel and Chinese characters. The figure appears three-dimensional, bursting out of the flat graphic poster frame.

Background: An ancient Western Regions frontier setting featuring rocky desert terrain, distant mountains, silhouettes of cavalry and caravans on the left, and a massive fortified fortress gate on the right with military banners, scaffolding, and guards. A weathered war banner hangs in the upper right. The environment evokes diplomacy, military conquest, and Silk Road expeditions.

Left Typography Block: Very large vertical black brush calligraphy title reading "[班超]" on the upper left. Beneath it, smaller vertical Chinese biographical text indicating birthplace, military role, and lifespan (32—102), accented by a red seal stamp.

Floating Archive Cards: Exactly 8 translucent glass-like historical archive cards framing the character, featuring thin gold borders, tiny corner rivets, Chinese descriptive text, and faded monochrome documentary illustrations:
1) Top center: labeled "01" and "73", abandoning the pen to join the army;
2) Left-middle: labeled "02" and "73", diplomatic mission to the Western Regions;
3) Top right: labeled "03" and "91", pacifying the Northern Xiongnu;
4) Right-middle: labeled "04" and "95", suppressing local rebellion;
5) Lower-left-middle: labeled "05" and "96", establishing the Protectorate of the Western Regions;
6) Bottom-left: labeled "06", governing forty years and uniting regional states;
7) Lower-right-middle: labeled "07", reopening and securing the Silk Road;
8) Bottom-right: labeled "08" and "102", returning to Luoyang in old age.

Bottom Timeline: A sleek horizontal gold timeline along the lower edge with milestone dots and Chinese text: 32 birth, 73 expedition west, 91 northern campaign, 95 suppression, 96 protectorate established, 102 return to Luoyang.

Visual Style & Atmosphere: High-detail 3D realism merged with museum exhibition infographics, sepia-gold and smoky gray historical palette, dramatic rim backlight, volumetric dust, atmospheric battlefield haze, and elegant gold linework. No English text.

